@page
@model IndexModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "A little more care. A lot less to remember.";
    var startPage = Model.IsLoggedIn ? "/Home" : "/Signup";
}

<div class="pack-landing" id="top">
    <section class="pack-hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="pack-container pack-hero-copy" data-reveal>
            <p class="pack-eyebrow">EVERY PET. EVERY PERSON. EVERY DAY.</p>
            <h1 id="hero-title">Big love.<br /><span>Little details, handled.</span></h1>
            <p class="pack-lead">From the first potty break to the next vet visit.<br class="d-none d-sm-block" /> One home for everything that goes into caring for your pack.</p>
            <div class="pack-actions">
                <a asp-page="@startPage" class="pack-button">Get started <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
                @if (!Model.IsLoggedIn)
                {
                    <a asp-page="/Login" class="pack-text-link">Take a closer look <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
        <figure class="pack-hero-product pack-container" data-hero-product>
            <div class="pack-window">
                <div class="pack-window-bar" aria-hidden="true"><span class="pack-window-dots">● ● ●</span><span>PackTracker / Your daily dashboard</span><span>↗</span></div>
                <img src="~/images/landing/dashboard.jpg" asp-append-version="true" width="1265" height="712" fetchpriority="high" alt="PackTracker dashboard showing Scout and Juniper, and quick potty logging." />
            </div>
            <figcaption>Actual PackTracker screens. A fictional pack, for a little inspiration.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div class="pack-hero-note"><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span> A closer look at a calmer routine</div>
    </section>

    <section class="pack-intro pack-container" id="features" aria-labelledby="intro-title">
        <p class="pack-eyebrow" data-reveal>THE WHOLE PICTURE</p>
        <h2 id="intro-title" data-reveal>They have your heart.<br /><span>Give their care a home.</span></h2>
        <p data-reveal>Potty breaks. Medication doses. That thing you wanted to ask the vet. Bring the everyday moments and the important records together, for every pet and everyone who cares for them.</p>
        <div class="pack-index" aria-label="Explore the app" data-reveal>
            <a href="#daily-care">01 <span>Daily care</span></a><a href="#health-history">02 <span>Health</span></a><a href="#medication-care">03 <span>Medications</span></a><a href="#vet-care">04 <span>Vet visits</span></a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pack-tour" aria-label="A tour of PackTracker">
        <div class="pack-tour-inner pack-container">
            <div class="pack-chapters">
                <article class="pack-chapter" id="daily-care" data-chapter="0">
                    <p class="pack-eyebrow">01 / THE EVERYDAY</p>
                    <h2>Small moments.<br /><span>All accounted for.</span></h2>
                    <p>See your whole pack at a glance. Log potty breaks, add care notes, and see when each pet last went. Their daily routine, without the guesswork.</p>
                    <ul><li>Individual profiles for every pet</li><li>Quick pee and poop logging</li><li>Activity history with who recorded it</li></ul>
                    <img class="pack-mobile-shot" src="~/images/landing/dashboard.jpg" asp-append-version="true" width="1265" height="712" loading="lazy" alt="Daily dashboard with two pet profiles and care activity." />
                </article>
                <article class="pack-chapter" id="health-history" data-chapter="1">
                    <p class="pack-eyebrow">02 / THEIR HEALTH STORY</p>
                    <h2>Remember the details.<br /><span>See the bigger picture.</span></h2>
                    <p>Keep symptoms, incidents, medication activity, and vet visits in one health history. Find the details you need by pet, date, or event.</p>
                    <ul><li>Symptom and incident notes</li><li>Severity, triggers, and recovery details</li><li>Grouped history or a chronological timeline</li></ul>
                    <img class="pack-mobile-shot" src="~/images/landing/health.jpg" asp-append-version="true" width="1265" height="712" loading="lazy" alt="Scout’s health overview, medication adherence, and health history." />
                </article>
                <article class="pack-chapter" id="medication-care" data-chapter="2">
                    <p class="pack-eyebrow">03 / A STEADIER ROUTINE</p>
                    <h2>Less “was that given?”<br /><span>More peace of mind.</span></h2>
                    <p>Keep medication instructions and schedules together. Record taken, skipped, or missed doses, with notes and a clear history of who gave what.</p>
                    <ul><li>Flexible medication schedules</li><li>Dose status and administration notes</li><li>Adherence at a glance</li></ul>
                    <img class="pack-mobile-shot" src="~/images/landing/medications.jpg" asp-append-version="true" width="1265" height="712" loading="lazy" alt="Medication schedule showing upcoming doses and recorded doses." />
                </article>
                <article class="pack-chapter" id="vet-care" data-chapter="3">
                    <p class="pack-eyebrow">04 / BEFORE, DURING, AND AFTER</p>
                    <h2>A better home<br /><span>for every vet visit.</span></h2>
                    <p>From the appointment to the follow-up, keep the whole visit together. Save clinic details, visit summaries, vaccination records, and documents where you can find them.</p>
                    <ul><li>Upcoming appointments and reminders</li><li>Visit notes and follow-up instructions</li><li>Invoices, lab results, and other attachments</li></ul>
                    <img class="pack-mobile-shot" src="~/images/landing/vet-visits.jpg" asp-append-version="true" width="1265" height="712" loading="lazy" alt="Vet visits screen with an upcoming checkup and clinic details." />
                </article>
            </div>
            <div class="pack-stage" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="pack-stage-glow"></div>
                <div class="pack-stage-window">
                    <div class="pack-window-bar"><span class="pack-window-dots">● ● ●</span><span data-stage-label>Daily care</span><span>PackTracker</span></div>
                    <div class="pack-stage-images">
                        <img class="is-active" data-screen="0" src="~/images/landing/dashboard.jpg" asp-append-version="true" width="1265" height="712" alt="" />
                        <img data-screen="1" src="~/images/landing/health.jpg" asp-append-version="true" width="1265" height="712" loading="lazy" alt="" />
                        <img data-screen="2" src="~/images/landing/medications.jpg" asp-append-version="true" width="1265" height="712" loading="lazy" alt="" />
                        <img data-screen="3" src="~/images/landing/vet-visits.jpg" asp-append-version="true" width="1265" height="712" loading="lazy" alt="" />
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="pack-stage-status"><span data-stage-count>01 / 04</span><div class="pack-progress"><i data-tour-progress></i></div><span>Made for real life</span></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pack-reports" aria-labelledby="reports-title">
        <div class="pack-container">
            <div class="pack-report-copy" data-reveal><p class="pack-eyebrow">FROM EVERYDAY NOTES TO THE NEXT CONVERSATION</p><h2 id="reports-title">Walk into the vet’s office<br /><span>with the story so far.</span></h2><p>Bring medications, dose history, health events, and past visits into a printable care report. Choose a date range and add the questions you don’t want to forget.</p></div>
            <figure class="pack-report-visual" data-reveal><img src="~/images/landing/reports.jpg" asp-append-version="true" width="1265" height="712" loading="lazy" alt="Printable care report for Scout, with a date range, medication summary, and questions for the vet." /><figcaption>The details you’ve collected. Ready for a more useful conversation.</figcaption></figure>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pack-together pack-container" aria-labelledby="together-title">
        <div data-reveal><p class="pack-eyebrow">ONE PACK. A SHARED ROUTINE.</p><h2 id="together-title">Care is better<br /><span>when it’s shared.</span></h2><p>Invite your household to care for the same pets from their own accounts. Give members and caregivers the right role, and keep everyone working from the same care history.</p></div>
        <div class="pack-details" data-reveal>
            <article><span aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><h3>Every pet belongs.</h3><p>Individual profiles, photos, and records keep a multi-pet household organized.</p></div></article>
            <article><span aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><h3>Everyone stays in the loop.</h3><p>Shared records and care attribution make handoffs easier.</p></div></article>
            <article><span aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><h3>Make yourself at home.</h3><p>Light and dark modes, account settings, and a household plan in one place.</p></div></article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pack-final" aria-labelledby="final-title"><div class="pack-container" data-reveal><p class="pack-eyebrow">MORE TIME FOR THE GOOD STUFF</p><h2 id="final-title">A little more together.<br /><span>A lot less to remember.</span></h2><p>Make room for a calmer kind of pet care.</p><a asp-page="@startPage" class="pack-button">Get started <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
    <footer class="pack-footer pack-container"><a href="#top" class="pack-wordmark">🐾 PackTracker</a><p>Thoughtful care. For your whole pack.</p><span>© @DateTime.Now.Year PackTracker</span><a asp-page="/Privacy">Privacy</a></footer>
</div>

@section Scripts {
    <script src="~/js/landing.js" asp-append-version="true" defer></script>
}
